Subject: [PATCH] vayu_wifi W25o: tell Apple80211 the station exists and has joined, and a DHCP
 fallback that configures en0 (vayu_wifi_dhcp=2)

Base: /mnt/ramdisk/ds-wifi2 as run 145915 (kernel mach-wifi25n; TX slot fix, kernel DHCP off).

Why iOS sent nothing in 145915 while it did DHCP in 143839: on the kernel side two things were
missing, both seen in the logs of both runs -- "apple80211: the station says:" never printed a
power/join/link event, and the station boundary (hakios_sta_attach) appeared only at S4, after the
association, so during the scan and the join wifid answered its Apple80211 requests with "no
station".  configd makes a network service for en0 from the IOKit objects (hakios.wlan.cpp) and
the link event (hakios_net_link_state, posted at S4), but iOS's Wi-Fi side learns that the
interface is powered and associated through Apple80211 events and the state request.

Changes:
 - bsd/dev/vayu_wifi_net.c: vayu_net_sta_attach() -- attached as soon as WMI READY gives the MAC
   (bsd/dev/vayu_wifi_scan.c, before the passive scan; again from vayu_wifi_sta.c), posts
   HAKIOS_STA_POWER.  sta_state() reports IDLE (radio on) from then on, JOINED once the keys are
   in, with SSID, BSSID, frequency and rssi of the join.  At S4 the station posts
   HAKIOS_STA_JOIN_DONE and HAKIOS_STA_LINK(1), which is what wifid turns into the link-changed /
   SSID / BSSID events for configd.
 - vayu_wifi_dhcp=2: the fallback.  iOS's configd gets 30 s from the link coming up; if en0 has no
   usable IPv4 address by then (hakios_net_has_ipv4(), bsd/dev/hakios.net.c: not 0.0.0.0, not
   169.254/16), the kernel client starts.  On ACK it gives en0 the address, netmask and broadcast
   (SIOCAIFADDR, as vayu_usbnet_ecm.c does for en2), brings it up and adds the default route via
   the lease's router (rtrequest RTM_ADD), and the line says "... (fallback)".  If iOS did get an
   address, the fallback says so and stays off.  vayu_wifi_dhcp=1 still starts the client at once.
 - job 1011 runs with vayu_wifi_dhcp=2 (iOS first, kernel only as the safety net).

Expected: "apple80211: the station says: power, 1" and "the link, 1" around S4, wifid's state
request answering JOINED with the SSID/frequency/rssi, configd's DHCP on en0; if 30 s pass with no
address: "no IPv4 on en0 after 30 s, fallback client on", "OK bound ... (fallback)", "OK address
en0 ...", "OK default route via ...".

